('app_26b6b382', '18', 'Test 2', NULL, NULL, '02_Renata_Alcott_CIO.pdf', 'Renata Alcott\nChief Information Officer\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | +60 12 345 9911  | renata.alcott@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/renataalcott-demo\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nHealthcare IT executive with 20 years driving digital transformation across multi-site hospital networks. Specializes in\nEHR modernization, clinical systems integration, and enterprise cybersecurity for regulated environments. Recognized\nfor aligning IT investment with patient outcomes and regulatory compliance (HIPAA-equivalent, PDPA).\nCORE COMPETENCIES\nDigital Health Transformation  | EHR/EMR Systems (Epic, Cerner)  | Healthcare Data Privacy  | Enterprise Architecture\n | IT Governance & Risk  | Vendor & Contract Management  | Business Continuity Planning  | Stakeholder & Board\nReporting\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nChief Information Officer — Meridian Regional Health Network\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Feb 2017 – Present\n Oversee IT strategy and USD 45M annual budget across a 12-hospital, 6,000-bed network serving 2.4M patients\nannually.\n Led enterprise EHR rollout across all facilities, reducing duplicate diagnostic testing by 28% and improving\ndischarge time by 19%.\n Rebuilt cybersecurity program following a 2018 phishing incident; achieved zero reportable breaches in 6\nconsecutive years.\n Chaired the Digital Health Steering Committee reporting directly to the Board of Directors.\nVP of Information Technology — Coral Bay Medical Group\nPenang, MY  | Sep 2011 – Jan 2017\n Directed IT operations for 4-hospital group; implemented telehealth platform reaching 40,000 rural patients in year\none.\n Negotiated and managed vendor contracts, saving USD 3.2M over a 3-year technology refresh cycle.\nIT Director, Clinical Systems — St. Aldric Hospital\nSingapore  | Jun 2005 – Aug 2011\n Led clinical systems team of 22 supporting pharmacy, radiology, and laboratory information systems.\n Managed the hospital\'s first PACS im