s, email systems, and access permissions.\nMonitor system performance and perform scheduled backups and updates.\nManage and maintain office network infrastructure (LAN/WAN, routers, switches, Wi-Fi).\nCoordinate with external vendors for IT maintenance and system upgrades.\nMaintain company website, hosting, and domain management.\nManage IT asset inventory and equipment lifecycle tracking.\nSupport Microsoft 365 applications including Outlook, Teams, and SharePoint.\nLed end-to-end deployment of POS systems across multiple outlets in Malaysia, ensuring\nminimal downtime.\nManaged operations team, conducted technical training, and coordinated with vendors for\nhardware/software delivery.\nSupported deployment of 90 AI vending machines across 18 MRT stations; performed\nsystem integration and testing.\nEstablished post-deployment monitoring and performance optimization processes.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATIONADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: Hardware & Network Configuration (LAN, IP, DHCP, Routers, Switches) |\nWindows 7/8/10/11 | Microsoft 365 (Outlook, Teams, OneDrive) | MySQL | C++, HTML,\nJavaScript, CSS, PHP\nCertifications: AWS Cloud Practitioner, Omada Certified Network Administrator Wireless,\nRUCKUS Accelerated Certified Partner Program\nLanguages: English and Malay\nTECHNICAL SKILLSTECHNICAL SKILLS\nDesktop & Laptop Troubleshooting (Windows Environment)\nHardware Installation & Maintenance\nSoftware Installation & Configuration\nPrinter & Peripheral Support\nIT Asset & Inventory Management\nBackup & System Updates\nRouter & Switch Configuration (Intermediate)\nWi-Fi & Internet Connectivity Troubleshooting\nVPN & Remote Access Support (Intermediate)\nIT Support & SystemsIT Support & Systems\nNetwork & InfrastructureNetwork & Infrastructure\nMicrosoft 365 Administration\nOutlook & Email Management\nBasic Active Directory Knowledge\nContent Management Systems (CMS)\nHTML & Wix Website Management\nSQL Accounting (Basic)\nAutoCount (Basic)\nSystems & ToolsSystems & Tools\nMicrosoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)\nCanva\nAdobe Premiere Pro\nOther ToolsOther Tools\nEDUCATIONEDUCATION\nBSc (Hons) Information & Communication Technology BSc (Hons) Information & Communication Technology \nLimkokwing University of Creative Technology (LUCT), Cyberjaya\nCGPA: 3.71\nApr 2017 – Dec 2020\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM)Sijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM)\nSekolah Menengah Kebangsaan Puncak Alam\n Jan 2012 - Dec 2016\nChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Antigravity\nPrompt Engineering\nLLM Applications\nAI Workflow Automation\nAI & Generative AIAI & Generative AI', 'MUHAMMAD DANIAL ASYRAAF BIN AZLANMUHAMMAD DANIAL ASYRAAF BIN AZLAN\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARYPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nSenior IT Specialist with hands-on experience in IT infrastructure, Microsoft 365, cloud operations,\nsystem integration, and AI-powered business solutions. Experienced in leveraging LLMs such as\nChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Antigravity to develop an AI Resume Screening System that\nautomates candidate parsing, scoring, ranking, and pre-interview assessments. Skilled in technical\nsupport, network administration, POS deployment, and vendor coordination, with a strong\ncommitment to delivering innovative and reliable IT solutions.\nWORK EXPERIENCEWORK EXPERIENCE\nSenior IT Specialist, ARB Berhad Senior IT Specialist, ARB Berhad 	Jul 2023 – Present\nJunior IT Specialist, ARB Berhad Junior IT Specialist, ARB Berhad \nAdministered virtual online voting platform, ensuring secure, stable, and compliant\noperations.\nCoordinated with clients, resellers, and developers for product customization and\nenhancements.\nProvided internal IT support (network setup, O365, hardware troubleshooting, backups,\nCCTV, asset management).\nJun 2022 – Jun 2023\nIT Executive Leadership Trainee, Telekom Malaysia IT Executive Leadership Trainee, Telekom Malaysia \nManaged Return Order Tracker (ROT) portal and performed data analysis to improve\noperational efficiency.\nApr 2021 – Nov 2021Bandar Puncak Alam, Selangor, Malaysia • +6017-341 2403 • [REDACTED EMAIL] \nDeveloped an AI-powered recruitment platform using ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and\nAntigravity.\nAutomated resume parsing, candidate scoring, and ranking based on job requirements.\nEnabled HR to shortlist top candidates and automate questionnaire and video introduction\nrequests.\nReduced manual resume screening through AI-assisted candidate evaluation.\nInstall, configure, and maintain desktops, laptops, printers, and office IT equipment.\nAdminister user accounts, email systems, and access permissions.\nMonitor system performance and perform scheduled backups and updates.\nManage and maintain office network infrastructure (LAN/WAN, routers, switches, Wi-Fi).\nCoordinate with external vendors for IT maintenance and system upgrades.\nMaintain company website, hosting, and domain management.\nManage IT asset inventory and equipment lifecycle tracking.\nSupport Microsoft 365 applications including Outlook, Teams, and SharePoint.\nLed end-to-end deployment of POS systems across multiple outlets in Malaysia, ensuring\nminimal downtime.\nManaged operations team, conducted technical training, and coordinated with vendors for\nhardware/software delivery.\nSupported deployment of 90 AI vending machines across 18 MRT stations; performed\nsystem integration and testing.\nEstablished post-deployment monitoring and performance optimization processes.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATIONADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: Hardware & Network Configuration (LAN, IP, DHCP, Routers, Switches) |\nWindows 7/8/10/11 | Microsoft 365 (Outlook, Teams, OneDrive) | MySQL | C++, HTML,\nJavaScript, CSS, PHP\nCertifications: AWS Cloud Practitioner, Omada Certified Network Administrator Wireless,\nRUCKUS Accelerated Certified Partner Program\nLanguages: English and Malay\nTECHNICAL SKILLSTECHNICAL SKILLS\nDesktop & Laptop Troubleshooting (Windows Environment)\nHardware Installation & Maintenance\nSoftware Installation & Configuration\nPrinter & Peripheral Support\nIT Asset & Inventory Management\nBackup & System Updates\nRouter & Switch Configuration (Intermediate)\nWi-Fi & Internet Connectivity Troubleshooting\nVPN & Remote Access Support (Intermediate)\nIT Support & SystemsIT Support & Systems\nNetwork & InfrastructureNetwork & Infrastructure\nMicrosoft 365 Administration\nOutlook & Email Management\nBasic Active Directory Knowledge\nContent Management Systems (CMS)\nHTML & Wix Website Management\nSQL Accounting (Basic)\nAutoCount (Basic)\nSystems & ToolsSystems & Tools\nMicrosoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)\nCanva\nAdobe Premiere Pro\nOther ToolsOther Tools\nEDUCATIONEDUCATION\nBSc (Hons) Information & Communication Technology BSc (Hons) Information & Communication Technology \nLimkokwing University of Creative Technology (LUCT), Cyberjaya\nCGPA: 3.71\nApr 2017 – Dec 2020\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM)Sijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM)\nSekolah Menengah Kebangsaan Puncak Alam\n Jan 2012 - Dec 2016\nChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Antigravity\nPrompt Engineering\nLLM Applications\nAI Workflow Automation\nAI & Generative AIAI & Generative AI', '68', 'Good', 'You have a solid technical foundation bridging IT infrastructure, network administration, and modern Generative AI workflow automation. However, your resume suffers from jumbled section hierarchy, duplicated technical skills, and inconsistent verb tenses across roles. With better bullet structure, clearer role-to-bullet alignment, and measurable business impact metrics, this can quickly become a standout resume.', '[\"Compelling blend of traditional IT support\\/infrastructure experience and modern Generative AI application development.\",\"Strong educational credential with a high CGPA (3.71) alongside recognized industry certifications like AWS Cloud Practitioner.\",\"Showcases impressive cross-functional initiatives such as deploying 90 AI vending machines across 18 MRT stations.\"]', '[\"Quantify bullet points with clear metrics (e.g., percentage of screening time reduced, number of POS outlets deployed, user support ticket resolution times).\",\"Consolidate the skills sections into a single, structured Technical Skills block rather than splitting across \'Additional Information\' and multiple sub-categories.\",\"Fix verb tense consistency in your current and past roles; use active past-tense verbs for completed projects and consistent present tense for ongoing duties.\",\"Remove high school education (SPM) now that you have a completed Bachelor\'s degree and several years of professional experience.\"]', 'The document shows duplicated headings and fragmented content blocks (such as AI skills appearing below Education). Ensure standard single-column flow with consistent spacing and clear section delineations.', '[\"Keep each job title, company name, location, and date range grouped strictly above its corresponding bullet points so ATS parsers attribute achievements to the correct employer.\",\"Avoid redundant text or split skill lists across multiple pages, which can confuse ATS keyword scrapers.\"]', '2026-09-04 09:59:12'),
('17', '20', 'AMIRUL FARIS RESUME.pdf', 'EDUCATION\nSUMMARY\nPROJECTS\nTRAINING AND CERTIFICATION\nMarch 2021-October 2023KOLEJ PROFESIONAL MARA BERANANG\nDiploma in Computer Science\nCGPA: 3.62\nMarch 2024-PresentUNIVERSITY KUALA LUMPUR MALAYSIAN INSTITUTE OF INFORMATION\nTECHNOLOGY (MIIT)\nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons.) in Software Engineering \nCGPA: 3.31\nSoftware Engineering undergraduate at UniKL MIIT with a 3.31 CGPA. Skilled in web development,\ndatabase management, AI integration, and software engineering principles. Experienced in developing\napplications using PHP, Laravel, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, and Google Cloud Firestore, alongside\nGenerative AI integration via the Google Gemini API. Actively seeking a Software Engineer internship from\nOctober 2026 to March 2027 to leverage technical expertise and drive impactful software solutions.\nAMIRUL FARIS BIN SUHAIMINSemarak, 54100, Kuala Lumpur |016-6034329 | amirulfaris077@gmail.com |linkedin.com/in/amirulfarisuhaimin \nATTENDANCE TRACKING SYSTEM FOR DOREMI SERVICES& RENTAL SDN. BHD.\nCo-developed an end-to-end HR attendance management solution with a two-person team,\ncomprising a web-based administrative portal and a partner-built mobile application.\nLed design and development of the web portal and backend architecture in PHP and Laravel, building\na responsive interface with JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nEngineered a hybrid database architecture combining SQL and Google Cloud Firestore (NoSQL) to\nsupport real-time data synchronization with the mobile application.\nIntegrated the Google Gemini API for Generative AI features, automating data processing tasks such\nas AI-assisted overtime verification.\nImplemented automated PDF report generation with DomPDF for attendance and administrative\nrecords.\nTechnologies Used: PHP, Laravel Framework, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore,\nGoogle Gemini API, DomPDF, Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API)\nGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate — core project management principles,\nstrategic planning, and Agile methodologies.\nDevSecOps Foundation Certification — Demonstrated understanding of secure software\ndevelopment, bridging the gap between development, IT operations, and security to ensure safe and\nefficient system deployments.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: PHP, Laravel, Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore\n(NoSQL), Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API), Web Prototyping, Database\nManagement, Front-End Development, Back-End Development\nMethodologies: Agile, IT Project Management, System Documentation, Software Engineering\nPrinciples\nSoft Skills: Customer Service, Interpersonal Communication, Team Collaboration, Problem-\nSolving, Adaptability, Sales and Promotion, Mobilegraphy\nLanguages: English, Malay\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nFeb 2026Event Promoter, The Aromania by Fragrance Festival Malaysia\nRepresented JOYRIA Beauty and GALAXY perfume brands at the Malaysia Muslim Festival, effectively\ncommunicating unique fragrance notes and profiles to visitors.\nEducated customers in discovering suitable scents by providing expert advice, demonstrating\nproducts, and tailoring personalized recommendations.\nMaximized high foot traffic in a fast-paced festival setting to actively engage potential buyers and\ngenerate promotional sales.\nJul 2024 - Oct 2024Retail Assistant, ZTE Mobile \nAdvised customers through product selections by leveraging expert-level knowledge of mobile\ndevices, consistently surpassing sales targets.\nProcessed efficient sales transactions, addressed customer inquiries, and accelerated overall store\nrevenue growth.\nCoordinated store visual merchandising standards and streamlined inventory management to ensure\noptimal product availability.\nAug 2023 - Jan 2024System Engineering Intern, Bastion Solution Sdn Bhd | Intern \nAdministered and optimized the government DDMS 2.0 system, ensuring high availability and\nseamless daily operations for end-users.\nExecuted continuous server monitoring to identify and proactively mitigate potential technical\ndisruptions.\nTroubleshot and resolved user-reported technical issues efficiently, providing vital support and\nelevating overall system satisfaction.\nREFERENCES INDUSTRIAL LINKAGES (IL)\nTs.Nurdatillah Hasim\nnurdatillah@unikl.edu.my \n(+60)17-5636371 \nNoor Suzieany Binti M Radzali\nnoorsuzieany@unikl.edu.my \n(+60)12-3664184\nLEADERSHIP & EXTRACURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\nLeader Team, TECHNOPRENEURSHIP \nTreasurer, Phantom Runners Club (PRC)\nMember, CREATIVE MULTIMEDIA CLUB\nMember, NETBALL CLUB\nMember, UniKL MIIT NETSYS CLUB\nParticipate Efootball Unikl E-Sport Carnival (UESC) 2025\nProfessional & Student Organizations\nRunner, Half Marathoner\nSports', 'EDUCATION\nSUMMARY\nPROJECTS\nTRAINING AND CERTIFICATION\nMarch 2021-October 2023KOLEJ PROFESIONAL MARA BERANANG\nDiploma in Computer Science\nCGPA: 3.62\nMarch 2024-PresentUNIVERSITY KUALA LUMPUR MALAYSIAN INSTITUTE OF INFORMATION\nTECHNOLOGY (MIIT)\nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons.) in Software Engineering \nCGPA: 3.31\nSoftware Engineering undergraduate at UniKL MIIT with a 3.31 CGPA. Skilled in web development,\ndatabase management, AI integration, and software engineering principles. Experienced in developing\napplications using PHP, Laravel, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, and Google Cloud Firestore, alongside\nGenerative AI integration via the Google Gemini API. Actively seeking a Software Engineer internship from\nOctober 2026 to March 2027 to leverage technical expertise and drive impactful software solutions.\nAMIRUL FARIS BIN SUHAIMINSemarak, 54100, Kuala Lumpur |[REDACTED PHONE] | [REDACTED EMAIL] |linkedin.com/in/amirulfarisuhaimin \nATTENDANCE TRACKING SYSTEM FOR DOREMI SERVICES& RENTAL SDN. BHD.\nCo-developed an end-to-end HR attendance management solution with a two-person team,\ncomprising a web-based administrative portal and a partner-built mobile application.\nLed design and development of the web portal and backend architecture in PHP and Laravel, building\na responsive interface with JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nEngineered a hybrid database architecture combining SQL and Google Cloud Firestore (NoSQL) to\nsupport real-time data synchronization with the mobile application.\nIntegrated the Google Gemini API for Generative AI features, automating data processing tasks such\nas AI-assisted overtime verification.\nImplemented automated PDF report generation with DomPDF for attendance and administrative\nrecords.\nTechnologies Used: PHP, Laravel Framework, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore,\nGoogle Gemini API, DomPDF, Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API)\nGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate — core project management principles,\nstrategic planning, and Agile methodologies.\nDevSecOps Foundation Certification — Demonstrated understanding of secure software\ndevelopment, bridging the gap between development, IT operations, and security to ensure safe and\nefficient system deployments.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: PHP, Laravel, Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore\n(NoSQL), Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API), Web Prototyping, Database\nManagement, Front-End Development, Back-End Development\nMethodologies: Agile, IT Project Management, System Documentation, Software Engineering\nPrinciples\nSoft Skills: Customer Service, Interpersonal Communication, Team Collaboration, Problem-\nSolving, Adaptability, Sales and Promotion, Mobilegraphy\nLanguages: English, Malay\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nFeb 2026Event Promoter, The Aromania by Fragrance Festival Malaysia\nRepresented JOYRIA Beauty and GALAXY perfume brands at the Malaysia Muslim Festival, effectively\ncommunicating unique fragrance notes and profiles to visitors.\nEducated customers in discovering suitable scents by providing expert advice, demonstrating\nproducts, and tailoring personalized recommendations.\nMaximized high foot traffic in a fast-paced festival setting to actively engage potential buyers and\ngenerate promotional sales.\nJul 2024 - Oct 2024Retail Assistant, ZTE Mobile \nAdvised customers through product selections by leveraging expert-level knowledge of mobile\ndevices, consistently surpassing sales targets.\nProcessed efficient sales transactions, addressed customer inquiries, and accelerated overall store\nrevenue growth.\nCoordinated store visual merchandising standards and streamlined inventory management to ensure\noptimal product availability.\nAug 2023 - Jan 2024System Engineering Intern, Bastion Solution Sdn Bhd | Intern \nAdministered and optimized the government DDMS 2.0 system, ensuring high availability and\nseamless daily operations for end-users.\nExecuted continuous server monitoring to identify and proactively mitigate potential technical\ndisruptions.\nTroubleshot and resolved user-reported technical issues efficiently, providing vital support and\nelevating overall system satisfaction.\nREFERENCES INDUSTRIAL LINKAGES (IL)\nTs.Nurdatillah Hasim\n[REDACTED EMAIL] \n(+60)17-5636371 \nNoor Suzieany Binti M Radzali\n[REDACTED EMAIL] \n(+60)12-3664184\nLEADERSHIP & EXTRACURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\nLeader Team, TECHNOPRENEURSHIP \nTreasurer, Phantom Runners Club (PRC)\nMember, CREATIVE MULTIMEDIA CLUB\nMember, NETBALL CLUB\nMember, UniKL MIIT NETSYS CLUB\nParticipate Efootball Unikl E-Sport Carnival (UESC) 2025\nProfessional & Student Organizations\nRunner, Half Marathoner\nSports', '72', 'Good', 'You have a solid technical foundation, impressive certifications, and a strong full-stack project that highlights modern tools like Laravel and the Google Gemini API. However, the section hierarchy is currently disorganized, with contact info misplaced and non-technical retail roles overshadowing your engineering internship. Reorganizing your layout to prioritize relevant software experience and adding measurable metrics will make your resume much more compelling to tech recruiters.', '[\"Demonstrates strong practical technical ability with a well-explained project integrating full-stack development, cloud databases, and Generative AI.\",\"Valuable industry-recognized certifications (DevSecOps Foundation and Google Project Management) that show initiative beyond the classroom.\",\"Clear, goal-oriented summary specifying your exact target internship dates and areas of expertise.\"]', '[\"Prioritize your System Engineering Intern experience at Bastion Solution above non-technical retail and event promoter roles.\",\"Add quantifiable results to your achievements (e.g., number of support tickets resolved, system uptime percentage, or processing time saved by AI automation).\",\"Remove the References section to save valuable real estate and replace it with a GitHub profile or portfolio link.\",\"Verify date accuracy and chronological ordering (e.g., \'Feb 2026\' appears out of sequence).\"]', 'Your contact header and name appear displaced in the body of the text; ensure your full contact information sits strictly at the top of page one in a clean single-column format.', '[\"Stick to standard section headings like \'Technical Skills\', \'Work Experience\', \'Projects\', and \'Education\' so ATS parsers categorize your details accurately.\",\"Group technical skills into clear categories (Languages, Frameworks, Cloud\\/Databases, Tools) rather than mixing soft skills and hobbies into the same section.\"]', '2026-09-04 10:16:30'),
